    <div class="screen" id="screen-tutorial" hidden>
        <div class="card" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="tut-title">
            <div class="eyebrow">How to play</div>
            <h2 id="tut-title">Stack your moves, then watch them play out</h2>

            <ul class="spec-list">
                <li><strong>Your end</strong> — <strong>you defend the BOTTOM goal and attack the TOP one.</strong>
                    Six a side: your keeper and five outfielders all start in your own half, so you always play
                    away from yourself.</li>
                <li><strong>The decision window</strong> — the moment either side wins the ball, the match pauses and
                    the ring in the centre circle starts draining. Nothing moves until it empties. You
                    stack <em>as many moves as you like</em> in that time; they all resolve together.</li>
                <li><strong>The pass</strong> — <em>drag from the ball-carrier onto a team-mate</em> to pass to them,
                    or <em>into empty space</em> to play it there. Anyone can receive, keeper included. The ball is
                    led into a team-mate's run, so a pass to a moving player meets them on the way.</li>
                <li><strong>The runs</strong> — <em>drag any of your players</em> to drop a ring where they should be
                    when the ball is played. Stack as many runners as you have players.</li>
                <li><strong>The shot</strong> — inside 30 units of goal, press <strong>SHOOT</strong> (or
                    <span class="keyhint">Space</span>, or double-tap the goal mouth) to stack a shot. The keeper
                    commits to a side, so <strong>aim across him</strong> — the far post is open. Outside that
                    range the button does nothing.</li>
                <li><strong>The save</strong> — defending, <em>drag your keeper to the dive point</em> to stack the
                    save. Leave it and the keeper dives on their own read.</li>
                <li><strong>Closing the window</strong> — press <strong>MOVES DONE</strong> (or
                    <span class="keyhint">Enter</span>). The CPU has to be ready too: if it has finished and you
                    have not, the board <em>stays frozen</em>. If you give no instruction at all, your side plays a
                    random pass.</li>
                <li><strong>The race</strong> — a pass only belongs to you if <em>the nearest player to the ball is
                    yours</em> when it lands. Send the wrong man and it spills loose, and the closest body from
                    either side goes for it. Whoever wins it opens the next window.</li>
                <li><strong>Keyboard</strong> — <span class="keyhint">Space</span> shoot ·
                    <span class="keyhint">Enter</span> moves done · <span class="keyhint">Esc</span> pause ·
                    <span class="keyhint">M</span> mute · <span class="keyhint">R</span> restart match.</li>
                <li><strong>Penalties</strong> — level at full time, press <strong>GO TO PENALTIES</strong>. Draw the aim
                    line, then draw the dive line: within the keeper's reach it is saved, otherwise it is a goal.</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="actions">
                <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary" id="btn-tut-close">GOT IT</button>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="screen" id="screen-pause" hidden>
